{"text":"<meta name=\"dash-one-writer\">\n<style>\n.jc { display: grid; gap: var(--cds-gap-xl); font-family: var(--font-anthropic-sans); }\n.jc-head { display: grid; gap: var(--cds-gap-sm); }\n.jc h1 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-anthropic-serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: var(--cds-font-size-title); }\n.jc-lede { margin: 0; max-width: 72ch; line-height: 1.55; }\n.jc h2 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--cds-font-size-heading); font-weight: var(--cds-font-weight-medium); }\n.jc-keys { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--cds-gap-sm) var(--cds-gap-lg); align-items: center; }\n.jc-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 14px; font-size: var(--cds-font-size-caption); }\n.jc-legend button { all: unset; cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 2px 4px; border-radius: 4px; }\n.jc-legend button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-fg); }\n.jc-legend button[aria-pressed=false] { opacity: .35; }\n.jc-legend i { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-block; }\n.jc-shapes { display: flex; gap: 14px; font-size: var(--cds-font-size-caption); color: var(--color-fg-muted); align-items: center; }\n.jc-shapes span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }\n.jc-shapes svg { display: block; }\n.jc-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--cds-gap-md); grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 30rem), 1fr)); }\n.jc-card { background: var(--color-panel); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-line); border-radius: var(--cds-radius); padding: var(--cds-pad-lg); display: grid; gap: var(--cds-gap-sm); align-content: start; min-width: 0; }\n.jc-note { margin: 0; font-size: var(--cds-font-size-caption); color: var(--color-fg-muted); line-height: 1.45; }\n.jc-sc { position: relative; min-height: 420px; }\n.jc-sc svg { display: block; }\n.jc-tip { position: absolute; pointer-events: none; background: var(--cds-surface-popover); border: 1px solid var(--cds-border); border-radius: var(--cds-radius); box-shadow: var(--cds-shadow-popover); padding: var(--cds-pad-xs) var(--cds-pad-sm); font-size: var(--cds-font-size-caption); max-width: 260px; z-index: 2; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n.jc-tip .k { color: var(--cds-text-secondary); }\n.jc-raw { overflow: auto; max-height: 560px; }\n.jc-raw table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--cds-font-size-caption); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n.jc-raw th { position: sticky; top: 0; background: var(--color-panel); text-align: right; padding: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-line); }\n.jc-raw th:nth-child(-n+3), .jc-raw td:nth-child(-n+3) { text-align: left; }\n.jc-raw th button { all: unset; cursor: pointer; display: block; padding: var(--cds-pad-xs) var(--cds-pad-sm); font-weight: var(--cds-font-weight-medium); white-space: nowrap; }\n.jc-raw th button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-fg); outline-offset: -2px; }\n.jc-raw td { padding: var(--cds-pad-xs) var(--cds-pad-sm); text-align: right; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-line); white-space: nowrap; }\n.jc [data-dash-source-state=refreshing] { opacity: .5; transition: opacity var(--cds-dur-slow); }\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"jc\">\n  <header class=\"jc-head\">\n    <h1>JPL compiler cold starts: O3 vs Os and Oz</h1>\n    <p class=\"jc-lede\">Four student JPL compilers, each built at O3, Os and Oz, timed once each from a cold start: the operating system's file cache was dropped right before every run, so the compiler binary and the 12 MB input were read from disk. Every dot is one compiler doing one job on one machine: across is its O3 time, up is its Os or Oz time. O3 is meant to be fastest, so a dot in the shaded triangle below the line is the unexpected result.</p>\n  </header>\n\n  <div class=\"jc-keys\">\n    <div class=\"jc-legend\" data-draw=\"legend\" data-source=\"jpl\" aria-label=\"Compilers; click to show or hide\"></div>\n    <div class=\"jc-shapes\">\n      <span><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"6\" r=\"5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-muted)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></circle></svg>Mac (M1 Pro)</span>\n      <span><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"var(--color-fg-muted)\"></rect></svg>x86 (Ryzen 5600X)</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"jc-grid\">\n    <section class=\"jc-card\" id=\"oz\">\n      <h2>Oz vs O3</h2>\n      <p class=\"jc-note\">One cold run each, log scale on both axes. Below the line, Oz ran faster than O3.</p>\n      <div class=\"jc-sc dash-skeleton\" data-draw=\"scatter\" data-y=\"oz_ms\" data-level=\"Oz\" data-source=\"jpl\"></div>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"jc-card\" id=\"os\">\n      <h2>Os vs O3</h2>\n      <p class=\"jc-note\">Same runs. The Zig compiler has no Os build (Zig only offers fast and small), so it appears only in the Oz chart.</p>\n      <div class=\"jc-sc dash-skeleton\" data-draw=\"scatter\" data-y=\"os_ms\" data-level=\"Os\" data-source=\"jpl\"></div>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n\n  <section class=\"jc-card\" id=\"raw\">\n    <h2>All runs</h2>\n    <p class=\"jc-note\">Each time is a single cold run, output sent to /dev/null. One run per point, so expect a few percent of noise. Code is the size of the binary's .text section. Click a header to sort.</p>\n    <div class=\"jc-raw\">\n      <table data-source=\"jpl\" data-row-key=\"compiler,machine,mode\">\n        <thead><tr>\n          <th data-field=\"compiler\"><button data-sort=\"compiler\">Compiler</button></th>\n          <th data-field=\"machine\"><button data-sort=\"machine\">Machine</button></th>\n          <th data-field=\"mode\"><button data-sort=\"mode\">Job</button></th>\n          <th data-field=\"o3_ms\"><button data-sort=\"o3_ms\">O3 ms</button></th>\n          <th data-field=\"os_ms\"><button data-sort=\"os_ms\">Os ms</button></th>\n          <th data-field=\"oz_ms\"><button data-sort=\"oz_ms\">Oz ms</button></th>\n          <th data-field=\"o3_text\"><button data-sort=\"o3_text\">O3 code</button></th>\n          <th data-field=\"os_text\"><button data-sort=\"os_text\">Os code</button></th>\n          <th data-field=\"oz_text\"><button data-sort=\"oz_text\">Oz code</button></th>\n        </tr></thead>\n        <tbody data-draw=\"rows\"></tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <details class=\"jc-note\">\n    <summary>How this was run</summary>\n    <p>Input: t3.jpl, 12,293,446 bytes, which all four typecheckers accept. Jobs are each compiler's -l (lex and print tokens), -p (parse and print the AST) and -t (typecheck and print) modes, with stdout sent to /dev/null, timed with hyperfine --runs 1 and no warmup; before each run --prepare dropped the file cache (sudo purge on macOS, echo 3 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches on Linux). The runs went in a shuffled order; the x86 runs under taskset -c 3. The three Rust compilers were built with cargo at opt-level 3, s and z plus -C target-cpu=native, keeping each Cargo.toml's other settings. The Zig compiler was built with zig 0.16 at ReleaseFast (shown as O3) and ReleaseSmall (shown as Oz). Each level produced identical output.</p>\n    <p>Mac: Apple M1 Pro, macOS. x86: AMD Ryzen 5 5600X, Ubuntu 24.04 under WSL2, pinned to one core. Pinned commits: Edward bf9d62c, Stefan (rjplc) d1f18f6, Henry (jpl-rs) 4acfca1.</p>\n  </details>\n</div>\n\n<script>\nwindow.jcOrder = ['Bobby (Zig)', 'Edward (Rust)', 'Stefan (Rust)', 'Henry (Rust)'];\nwindow.jcColor = (c) => dash.colors[Math.max(0, window.jcOrder.indexOf(c)) % dash.colors.length];\nwindow.jcHidden = new Set();\n\ndash.draw('legend', (el) => {\n  const D = dash.data('jpl');\n  el.replaceChildren();\n  if (D.status !== 'ok') { el.textContent = '—'; return; }\n  for (const c of window.jcOrder.filter((c) => D.data.some((r) => r.compiler === c))) {\n    const b = document.createElement('button');\n    b.type = 'button';\n    b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(!window.jcHidden.has(c)));\n    const i = document.createElement('i'); i.style.background = window.jcColor(c);\n    b.append(i, document.createTextNode(c));\n    b.onclick = () => { window.jcHidden.has(c) ? window.jcHidden.delete(c) : window.jcHidden.add(c); dash.draw('legend'); dash.draw('scatter'); };\n    el.appendChild(b);\n  }\n});\n\ndash.draw('scatter', (el) => {\n  const D = dash.data('jpl');\n  el.replaceChildren();\n  if (D.status !== 'ok') { el.textContent = '—'; el.classList.add('dash-skeleton'); return; }\n  el.classList.remove('dash-skeleton');\n  const fy = el.dataset.y, level = el.dataset.level;\n  const all = D.data.filter((r) => r.o3_ms > 0 && (r.os_ms > 0 || r.oz_ms > 0));\n  const rows = D.data.filter((r) => r.o3_ms > 0 && r[fy] > 0 && !window.jcHidden.has(r.compiler));\n  const W = Math.max(300, el.clientWidth), H = Math.min(560, Math.max(340, W * 0.8));\n  const m = { t: 12, r: 14, b: 46, l: 58 };\n  const vals = all.flatMap((r) => [r.o3_ms, r.os_ms, r.oz_ms]).filter((v) => v > 0);\n  const lo = d3.min(vals) * 0.9, hi = d3.max(vals) * 1.1;\n  const sx = d3.scaleLog([lo, hi], [m.l, W - m.r]), sy = d3.scaleLog([lo, hi], [H - m.b, m.t]);\n  const tf = (v) => v >= 1000 ? d3.format('~g')(v / 1000) + ' s' : d3.format('~g')(v) + ' ms';\n  const cand = [];\n  for (let e = Math.floor(Math.log10(lo)); e <= Math.ceil(Math.log10(hi)); e++) for (const k of [1, 1.5, 2, 3, 5, 7]) { const v = k * 10 ** e; if (v >= lo && v <= hi) cand.push(v); }\n  const ticks = [];\n  for (const v of cand) if (!ticks.length || sx(v) - sx(ticks[ticks.length - 1]) >= 44) ticks.push(v);\n  const svg = d3.select(el).append('svg').attr('width', '100%').attr('viewBox', `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr('height', H);\n  el.style.minHeight = H + 'px';\n  const x0 = m.l, x1 = W - m.r, y0 = m.t, y1 = H - m.b;\n  // Unexpected: the size level ran faster (below the diagonal).\n  svg.append('path').attr('d', `M${sx(lo)},${sy(lo)} L${sx(hi)},${sy(hi)} L${x1},${y1} L${x0},${y1} Z`).attr('fill', 'var(--color-warn)').attr('fill-opacity', 0.12);\n  const grid = svg.append('g');\n  grid.selectAll('line.gy').data(ticks).join('line').attr('class', 'gy').attr('x1', x0).attr('x2', x1).attr('y1', sy).attr('y2', sy).attr('stroke', 'var(--cds-chart-grid)');\n  grid.selectAll('line.gx').data(ticks).join('line').attr('class', 'gx').attr('y1', y0).attr('y2', y1).attr('x1', sx).attr('x2', sx).attr('stroke', 'var(--cds-chart-grid)');\n  svg.append('line').attr('x1', x0).attr('x2', x1).attr('y1', y1).attr('y2', y1).attr('stroke', 'var(--cds-chart-axis)');\n  svg.append('line').attr('x1', x0).attr('x2', x0).attr('y1', y0).attr('y2', y1).attr('stroke', 'var(--cds-chart-axis)');\n  const lab = svg.append('g').attr('font-size', 11).attr('fill', 'var(--color-fg-muted)');\n  lab.selectAll('text.tx').data(ticks).join('text').attr('class', 'tx').attr('x', sx).attr('y', y1 + 15).attr('text-anchor', 'middle').text(tf);\n  lab.selectAll('text.ty').data(ticks.filter((v, i) => i === 0 || sy(ticks[i - 1]) - sy(v) >= 16)).join('text').attr('class', 'ty').attr('x', x0 - 6).attr('y', sy).attr('dy', '0.35em').attr('text-anchor', 'end').text(tf);\n  svg.append('text').attr('x', (x0 + x1) / 2).attr('y', H - 8).attr('text-anchor', 'middle').attr('font-size', 12).attr('fill', 'var(--color-fg)').text('O3 time →');\n  svg.append('text').attr('transform', `translate(14,${(y0 + y1) / 2}) rotate(-90)`).attr('text-anchor', 'middle').attr('font-size', 12).attr('fill', 'var(--color-fg)').text(`${level} time →`);\n  svg.append('line').attr('x1', sx(lo)).attr('y1', sy(lo)).attr('x2', sx(hi)).attr('y2', sy(hi)).attr('stroke', 'var(--cds-chart-reference)').attr('stroke-dasharray', '4 3');\n  svg.append('text').attr('x', x1 - 6).attr('y', y1 - 8).attr('text-anchor', 'end').attr('font-size', 12).attr('font-weight', 600).attr('fill', 'var(--color-fg-muted)').text(`${level} faster: unexpected`);\n  svg.append('text').attr('x', x0 + 8).attr('y', y0 + 14).attr('font-size', 12).attr('font-weight', 600).attr('fill', 'var(--color-fg-muted)').text('O3 faster: expected');\n  const isX86 = (r) => r.machine.startsWith('x86');\n  const sym = d3.symbol().size(80);\n  svg.append('g').selectAll('path').data(rows).join('path')\n    .attr('transform', (r) => `translate(${sx(r.o3_ms)},${sy(r[fy])})`)\n    .attr('d', (r) => sym.type(isX86(r) ? d3.symbolSquare : d3.symbolCircle)())\n    .attr('fill', (r) => isX86(r) ? window.jcColor(r.compiler) : 'var(--color-panel)')\n    .attr('stroke', (r) => window.jcColor(r.compiler)).attr('stroke-width', 2);\n  const ring = svg.append('circle').attr('r', 10).attr('fill', 'none').attr('stroke', 'var(--color-fg)').attr('stroke-width', 2).style('display', 'none');\n  const tip = d3.select(el).append('div').attr('class', 'jc-tip').style('display', 'none');\n  const pts = rows.map((r) => [sx(r.o3_ms), sy(r[fy])]);\n  const del = d3.Delaunay.from(pts);\n  const ms = (v) => d3.format(',.1f')(v) + ' ms';\n  const hide = () => { tip.style('display', 'none'); ring.style('display', 'none'); };\n  svg.append('rect').attr('x', x0).attr('y', y0).attr('width', x1 - x0).attr('height', y1 - y0).attr('fill', 'transparent')\n    .on('pointermove', (ev) => {\n      if (!rows.length) return;\n      const [px, py] = d3.pointer(ev, svg.node());\n      const sc = W / svg.node().getBoundingClientRect().width;\n      const i = del.find(px, py), [cx, cy] = pts[i];\n      if (Math.hypot(cx - px, cy - py) > 40 * sc) return hide();\n      const r = rows[i], q = r[fy] / r.o3_ms;\n      ring.style('display', null).attr('cx', cx).attr('cy', cy);\n      tip.style('display', null); tip.selectAll('*').remove();\n      tip.append('div').attr('class', 'k').text(`${r.compiler} · ${r.mode} · ${r.machine}`);\n      const sdk = fy.replace('_ms', '_sd'), pm = (v) => v == null ? '' : ` ± ${d3.format(',.1f')(v)}`;\n      tip.append('div').text(`O3 ${ms(r.o3_ms)}${pm(r.o3_sd)}`);\n      tip.append('div').text(`${level} ${ms(r[fy])}${pm(r[sdk])}`);\n      tip.append('div').style('font-weight', 600).text(q < 1 ? `${level} ${d3.format('.1%')(1 - q)} faster` : `${level} ${d3.format('.2f')(q)}× O3's time`);\n      // Beside the dot, never over it: right of it if there is room, else left; centered on it vertically.\n      const bx = cx / sc, by = cy / sc, gap = 18;\n      const tw = tip.node().offsetWidth, th = tip.node().offsetHeight;\n      const left = bx + gap + tw <= el.clientWidth ? bx + gap : Math.max(0, bx - gap - tw);\n      const top = Math.max(0, Math.min(by - th / 2, el.clientHeight - th));\n      tip.style('left', left + 'px').style('top', top + 'px');\n    })\n    .on('pointerleave', hide);\n});\n</script>\n\n<script>\nwindow.jcSort = { key: 'compiler', dir: 1 };\ndocument.querySelectorAll('.jc-raw th button[data-sort]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {\n  const k = b.dataset.sort;\n  window.jcSort = { key: k, dir: window.jcSort.key === k ? -window.jcSort.dir : (/_(ms|text)$/.test(k) ? -1 : 1) };\n  document.querySelectorAll('.jc-raw th').forEach((th) => th.removeAttribute('aria-sort'));\n  b.parentElement.setAttribute('aria-sort', window.jcSort.dir > 0 ? 'ascending' : 'descending');\n  dash.draw('rows');\n}));\n\ndash.draw('rows', (tb) => {\n  const D = dash.data('jpl');\n  tb.replaceChildren();\n  if (D.status !== 'ok') return;\n  const { key, dir } = window.jcSort, modes = ['lex', 'parse', 'typecheck'];\n  const base = (a, b) => window.jcOrder.indexOf(a.compiler) - window.jcOrder.indexOf(b.compiler) || a.machine.localeCompare(b.machine) || modes.indexOf(a.mode) - modes.indexOf(b.mode);\n  const rows = [...D.data].sort((a, b) => {\n    if (key === 'compiler') return dir * base(a, b);\n    if (key === 'machine' || key === 'mode') return dir * (String(a[key]).localeCompare(String(b[key])) || base(a, b));\n    if (a[key] == null) return 1; if (b[key] == null) return -1;\n    return dir * (a[key] - b[key]);\n  });\n  const f1 = d3.format(',.1f'), f0 = d3.format(',');\n  for (const r of rows) {\n    const tr = tb.insertRow();\n    tr.dataset.key = [r.compiler, r.machine, r.mode].map(encodeURIComponent).join(',');\n    [r.compiler, r.machine, r.mode, f1(r.o3_ms), r.os_ms == null ? '—' : f1(r.os_ms), f1(r.oz_ms), f0(r.o3_text), r.os_text == null ? '—' : f0(r.os_text), f0(r.oz_text)]\n      .forEach((c) => { tr.insertCell().textContent = c; });\n  }\n});\n</script>\n","edit":{"via":"claude","at":"2026-11-08T10:58:23.052Z"}}